---
import LandingLayout from "../layouts/LandingLayout.astro";

const lastUpdated = "25 February 2026";
---

<LandingLayout
  title="Privacy Policy"
  description="How Future of Dev collects and uses data, and your rights under GDPR."
>
  <div class="max-w-2xl mx-auto px-6 pt-16 md:pt-24 pb-24">

    <div class="mb-10">
      <p class="text-xs font-mono uppercase tracking-widest text-muted-foreground mb-3">Legal</p>
      <h1 class="text-3xl md:text-4xl font-bold tracking-tight mb-3">Privacy Policy</h1>
      <p class="text-sm text-muted-foreground">Last updated: {lastUpdated}</p>
    </div>

    <div class="prose-section space-y-10">

      <section>
        <h2>Who we are</h2>
        <p>
          Future of Dev (<a href="https://futureofdev.com">futureofdev.com</a>) is run by Luke Hennerley.
          We publish free courses, insights, and resources to help people navigate software careers in the AI era.
          You can reach us at <a href="mailto:luke@futureofdev.com">luke@futureofdev.com</a>.
        </p>
      </section>

      <section>
        <h2>What we collect and why</h2>

        <h3>Analytics (PostHog)</h3>
        <p>
          We use PostHog to understand how people use this site — which pages are visited, where people drop off,
          and how content performs. By default, PostHog runs in a cookieless, memory-only mode: no data is stored
          on your device and nothing persists between visits.
        </p>
        <p>
          If you accept cookies via the banner, PostHog switches to cookie-based tracking so we can recognise
          you across visits. In that mode, a random anonymous identifier is stored in a cookie on your device.
          No name or email is attached to this identifier unless you choose to share it (e.g. by subscribing
          to the newsletter).
        </p>
        <p>
          PostHog is self-hostable and we use their EU-based cloud (<code>eu.i.posthog.com</code>).
          Data does not leave the EU. See <a href="https://posthog.com/privacy" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">PostHog's privacy policy</a>.
        </p>

        <h3>Newsletter (Resend)</h3>
        <p>
          If you subscribe to our newsletter, we store your email address with Resend to send you updates.
          You can unsubscribe at any time via the link in any email. We do not sell or share your email
          with third parties. See <a href="https://resend.com/legal/privacy-policy" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">Resend's privacy policy</a>.
        </p>
        <p>
          When you subscribe, we also associate your email with your PostHog analytics profile (if PostHog
          is active in your session). This lets us understand the journey from visitor to subscriber.
          Your email is only linked to analytics data on devices where you have subscribed.
        </p>

        <h3>Course progress (Claude Academy)</h3>
        <p>
          If you take a course via Claude Academy and opt in to progress sharing, we collect anonymous
          lesson completion data: a randomly generated ID (no name, email, or device info), the phase and
          lesson numbers, and a timestamp. This data is stored in Supabase on EU-based infrastructure
          and is used solely to understand how students progress through the curriculum.
          You are asked for this consent explicitly before any data is sent.
        </p>
      </section>

      <section>
        <h2>Cookies</h2>
        <p>
          We only set cookies if you accept the cookie consent banner. The cookies we set are:
        </p>
        <ul>
          <li><strong>ph_*</strong> — PostHog analytics cookies. Store an anonymous distinct ID to recognise you across visits. No personal information is stored in the cookie itself.</li>
        </ul>
        <p>
          We also use <code>localStorage</code> to store your cookie preference (<code>ph_consent</code>)
          so we don't ask again on future visits.
        </p>
        <p>
          You can clear your consent at any time by clearing your browser's cookies and local storage for this site.
        </p>
      </section>

      <section>
        <h2>Your rights (GDPR)</h2>
        <p>If you are in the EU or UK, you have the right to:</p>
        <ul>
          <li><strong>Access</strong> — request a copy of any personal data we hold about you</li>
          <li><strong>Erasure</strong> — ask us to delete your data</li>
          <li><strong>Objection</strong> — object to processing based on legitimate interests</li>
          <li><strong>Portability</strong> — receive your data in a portable format</li>
          <li><strong>Withdraw consent</strong> — opt out of cookies at any time by clearing your browser storage</li>
        </ul>
        <p>
          To exercise any of these rights, email <a href="mailto:luke@futureofdev.com">luke@futureofdev.com</a>.
          We will respond within 30 days.
        </p>
      </section>

      <section>
        <h2>Third-party services</h2>
        <ul>
          <li><a href="https://posthog.com/privacy" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">PostHog</a> — analytics</li>
          <li><a href="https://resend.com/legal/privacy-policy" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">Resend</a> — email delivery</li>
          <li><a href="https://supabase.com/privacy" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">Supabase</a> — anonymous course progress data</li>
          <li><a href="https://www.sanity.io/legal/privacy" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">Sanity</a> — content management</li>
          <li><a href="https://www.cloudflare.com/privacypolicy/" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">Cloudflare</a> — hosting and delivery</li>
        </ul>
      </section>

      <section>
        <h2>Changes to this policy</h2>
        <p>
          We may update this policy from time to time. The date at the top of this page reflects the most
          recent revision. Continued use of the site after changes constitutes acceptance of the updated policy.
        </p>
      </section>

      <section>
        <h2>Contact</h2>
        <p>
          Questions about this policy? Email <a href="mailto:luke@futureofdev.com">luke@futureofdev.com</a>.
        </p>
      </section>

    </div>
  </div>
</LandingLayout>

<style>
  .prose-section h2 {
    font-size: 1.125rem;
    font-weight: 600;
    color: hsl(var(--foreground));
    margin-bottom: 0.75rem;
    padding-bottom: 0.5rem;
    border-bottom: 1px solid hsl(var(--border));
  }

  .prose-section h3 {
    font-size: 0.9375rem;
    font-weight: 600;
    color: hsl(var(--foreground));
    margin-top: 1.25rem;
    margin-bottom: 0.5rem;
  }

  .prose-section p {
    font-size: 0.9375rem;
    line-height: 1.75;
    color: hsl(var(--foreground) / 0.8);
    margin-bottom: 0.875rem;
  }

  .prose-section ul {
    list-style: disc;
    padding-left: 1.5rem;
    margin-bottom: 0.875rem;
    space-y: 0.25rem;
  }

  .prose-section li {
    font-size: 0.9375rem;
    line-height: 1.75;
    color: hsl(var(--foreground) / 0.8);
    margin-bottom: 0.25rem;
  }

  .prose-section a {
    color: hsl(var(--foreground));
    text-decoration: underline;
    text-underline-offset: 3px;
  }

  .prose-section a:hover {
    color: hsl(var(--primary));
  }

  .prose-section code {
    font-family: 'JetBrains Mono', monospace;
    font-size: 0.8125rem;
    background: hsl(var(--muted));
    padding: 0.125rem 0.375rem;
    border-radius: 0.25rem;
  }
</style>
